<title>UK: UPS launches European internet sites.</title>
<headline>UPS launches European internet sites.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>United Parcel Service said it has launched a series of five new European internet sites to allow local customers to easily access service information and track shipments throughout its worldwide network.</p>
<p>In a statement UPS said the new sites for France, Germany, Italy, Spain and UK include details on the local range of services, contact information and tracking capabilities in the local language.</p>
<p>Currently there are an average of 200,000 hits per day on the UPS' global site, with about 28,000 packages tracked daily.</p>
<p>Other European languages, will be added to the web site rapidly over the coming months, it said. - Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542 7706 Fax+44 171 542 5017</p>
